WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.848 --> 00:00:03.283
civilians remain, only five to

00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:05.685
ten residents are leaving each

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:05.952
day.

00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:07.821
Joining me is Leon Panetta to

00:00:07.954 --> 00:00:09.890
talk about this.

00:00:10.023 --> 00:00:10.624
Mr. Secretary, all great to have

00:00:10.757 --> 00:00:11.391
you on.

00:00:11.524 --> 00:00:13.760
It does seem to be a critical

00:00:13.894 --> 00:00:28.441
time for Ukrainian forces around

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:28.642
bakhmut.

00:00:28.775 --> 00:00:31.311
&gt;&gt; There's no question that

00:00:31.444 --> 00:00:33.380
there's psychological impact

00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:35.782
when the Russians are able to

00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:38.451
gain anything in the Ukraine

00:00:38.485 --> 00:00:39.352
these days.

00:00:39.486 --> 00:00:43.223
I'm not sure it's that important

00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:45.392
a strategic military target

00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:46.826
because it's been destroyed by

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:53.333
the Russians and turned into

00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:56.069
ashes and so I understand the

00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:58.138
game of trying to gain any

00:00:58.471 --> 00:00:59.806
territory you can.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.743
But I think this is more of a

00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:07.547
preliminary step for both sides

00:01:07.681 --> 00:01:09.616
in terms of getting ready for

00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:13.253
the next chapter in this war,

00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:15.622
which is going to involve some

00:01:15.755 --> 00:01:18.758
serious offensives on both

00:01:18.892 --> 00:01:21.528
sides, not just Russia but I

00:01:21.661 --> 00:01:26.099
think Ukraine will conduct an

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:27.233
offensive and I think it's going

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.002
to be a critical moment that

00:01:29.135 --> 00:01:30.503
will tell us a lot about the

00:01:30.503 --> 00:01:32.505
future of this war.

00:01:32.505 --> 00:01:33.540
&gt;&gt; Absolutely.

00:01:33.673 --> 00:01:36.009
And let's talk about China.

00:01:36.142 --> 00:01:42.515
It came up a lot on the Sunday

00:01:42.515 --> 00:01:42.882
talk shows earlier today.

00:01:43.016 --> 00:01:44.718
I have to ask in a draft budget

00:01:44.851 --> 00:01:45.552
report released this morning,

00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:49.322
China unveiled its annual

00:01:49.456 --> 00:01:53.059
military budget which showed an

00:01:53.193 --> 00:01:54.594
increase to $224 billion.

00:01:54.728 --> 00:01:56.529
China keeps ramping things up on

00:01:56.529 --> 00:01:56.863
the military front.

00:01:56.997 --> 00:01:58.131
How much of a concern does this

00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:00.533
need to be for the intelligence

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:05.572
community, for the Pentagon

00:02:05.705 --> 00:02:07.040
moving forward, do you think?

00:02:07.173 --> 00:02:10.210
&gt;&gt; Well, we have to pay

00:02:10.543 --> 00:02:13.380
attention to what China is

00:02:13.513 --> 00:02:15.648
doing.

00:02:15.782 --> 00:02:18.551
Obviously China is not just a

00:02:18.585 --> 00:02:21.421
competitor in the world but in

00:02:21.554 --> 00:02:24.557
many ways they're an adversary

00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:24.858
in the world.

00:02:24.991 --> 00:02:26.726
And we have to pay attention to

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.295
the amount of money that they're

00:02:29.429 --> 00:02:31.531
putting into defense, into

00:02:31.664 --> 00:02:33.299
space, what they're doing in

00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:36.002
terms of militarizing the south

00:02:36.136 --> 00:02:36.569
China sea.

00:02:36.703 --> 00:02:39.339
There are threats to Taiwan.

00:02:39.472 --> 00:02:42.609
So it is of concern.

00:02:42.742 --> 00:02:44.110
And our intelligence officials,

00:02:44.244 --> 00:02:47.814
our military officials have to

00:02:47.947 --> 00:02:49.416
constantly analyze what steps

00:02:49.549 --> 00:02:51.584
China is taking in order to be

00:02:51.718 --> 00:02:54.120
prepared to counter whatever

00:02:54.254 --> 00:02:54.921
they do.

00:02:55.055 --> 00:02:56.723
Look, the only way to deal with

00:02:56.856 --> 00:02:58.058
China is from strength.

00:02:58.191 --> 00:03:01.061
So it's very important that the

00:03:01.194 --> 00:03:01.895
United States make very clear

00:03:02.028 --> 00:03:07.400
where the lines are in terms of

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.269
Taiwan, in terms of the south

00:03:09.402 --> 00:03:09.736
China sea.

00:03:09.869 --> 00:03:14.607
In terms of just their defense

00:03:14.607 --> 00:03:16.209
buildup and where it should go.

00:03:16.609 --> 00:03:17.811
You would hope we could

00:03:17.944 --> 00:03:21.081
reestablish some kind of

00:03:21.214 --> 00:03:22.949
dialogue with China ultimately

00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:24.984
but we're not there yet and I

00:03:25.118 --> 00:03:26.152
suspect we're probably going to

00:03:26.286 --> 00:03:28.655
go through a very tense period

00:03:28.788 --> 00:03:29.522
in our relationship before

00:03:29.656 --> 00:03:31.825
hopefully we're able to talk to

00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:32.625
one another.

00:03:32.725 --> 00:03:35.762
&gt;&gt; And I hate to ask you about

00:03:35.895 --> 00:03:40.834
politics but let me do that.

00:03:40.967 --> 00:03:42.135
Former president Donald Trump

00:03:42.268 --> 00:03:47.474
won the CPAC straw poll,

00:03:47.607 --> 00:03:51.845
emphasized it's unscientific.

00:03:51.978 --> 00:03:52.645
He is leading in just about all

00:03:52.712 --> 00:03:54.180
the Republican polls and it's

00:03:54.314 --> 00:03:56.049
early in the process.

00:03:56.182 --> 00:03:57.650
What message would it send to

00:03:57.784 --> 00:03:59.586
the world if trump were to

00:03:59.719 --> 00:04:00.653
somehow able to get back into

00:04:00.787 --> 00:04:01.354
the white house?

00:04:01.488 --> 00:04:03.256
You are in addition being a wise

00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:05.024
elder when it comes to national

00:04:05.158 --> 00:04:05.658
security and intelligence

00:04:05.792 --> 00:04:07.127
matters, you know this game as

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.661
well as just about anybody,

00:04:08.728 --> 00:04:09.562
former white house chief of

00:04:09.696 --> 00:04:10.763
staff and so on.

00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:12.332
Do you think trump can do it

00:04:12.665 --> 00:04:14.667
again and what does that say to

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.035
the world that he's even in this

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:17.604
position right now?

00:04:17.737 --> 00:04:19.772
&gt;&gt; Well, I don't think we should

00:04:19.906 --> 00:04:20.673
kid ourselves.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:25.345
I think the reality is that he

00:04:25.478 --> 00:04:28.681
has support in the Republican

00:04:28.681 --> 00:04:31.351
party and that he could very

00:04:31.484 --> 00:04:33.153
well be the candidate for the

00:04:33.286 --> 00:04:33.820
Republican party.

00:04:33.953 --> 00:04:36.189
I think it would be a terrible

00:04:36.322 --> 00:04:39.159
message to send to the world if,

00:04:39.292 --> 00:04:41.261
in fact, he is a candidate again

00:04:41.394 --> 00:04:44.230
for president of the united

00:04:44.364 --> 00:04:47.467
States because I believe that

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.703
his whole first -- America first

00:04:50.703 --> 00:04:54.374
approach to foreign policy, his

00:04:54.707 --> 00:04:56.709
desire to essentially withdraw

00:04:56.776 --> 00:04:59.045
from the world in terms of a

00:04:59.179 --> 00:05:00.747
leadership position for the

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.715
United States would be

00:05:02.715 --> 00:05:03.082
devastating to our foreign

00:05:03.216 --> 00:05:04.717
policy at this point in time in

00:05:04.717 --> 00:05:07.253
the 21st century.

00:05:07.387 --> 00:05:13.693
Look, in the end I really -- I

00:05:13.826 --> 00:05:15.128
really believe that he's a loser

00:05:15.261 --> 00:05:17.597
and that even if he gets the

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.332
nomination, he will lose.

00:05:19.465 --> 00:05:20.733
But the mere fact that he would

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.870
be nominated by the Republican

00:05:24.003 --> 00:05:26.406
party would be a scary step in

00:05:26.739 --> 00:05:28.408
the 21st century.

00:05:28.741 --> 00:05:31.611
&gt;&gt; And just a quick follow, I

00:05:31.744 --> 00:05:32.946
think it would definitely mean a

00:05:33.079 --> 00:05:36.382
big change in how the U.S. Deals

00:05:36.749 --> 00:05:37.050
with Ukraine.

00:05:37.183 --> 00:05:39.052
&gt;&gt; Oh, my god.

00:05:39.185 --> 00:05:41.721
You know, we have just gone

00:05:41.854 --> 00:05:43.890
through a few years where

00:05:44.023 --> 00:05:48.428
fortunately we've been able to

00:05:48.761 --> 00:05:49.262
reestablish the United States'

00:05:49.395 --> 00:05:50.830
role as a world leader.

00:05:50.964 --> 00:05:52.765
And I think president Biden

00:05:52.765 --> 00:05:54.300
basically said to the world that

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.769
the United States is back and

00:05:56.803 --> 00:05:58.905
he's kind of -- he's made very

00:05:59.038 --> 00:06:00.773
clear that the United States

00:06:00.773 --> 00:06:03.643
working with our allies are

00:06:03.776 --> 00:06:07.747
going to be unified in

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.382
confronting adversaries like

00:06:09.515 --> 00:06:12.185
Putin and China and North Korea,

00:06:12.318 --> 00:06:12.986
Iran and others.

00:06:13.119 --> 00:06:15.088
And we have to be unified in the

00:06:15.221 --> 00:06:15.588
world.

00:06:15.722 --> 00:06:19.225
Look, it's a dangerous world.

00:06:19.359 --> 00:06:20.860
It's going to require the united

00:06:20.994 --> 00:06:23.229
States world leadership, and the

00:06:23.363 --> 00:06:24.797
last thing the United States

00:06:24.797 --> 00:06:25.765
needs do is to elect somebody

00:06:25.898 --> 00:06:27.166
like trump who doesn't want to

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.168
be a world leader, who ignores

00:06:29.302 --> 00:06:31.838
the rest of the world.

00:06:31.971 --> 00:06:33.706
It would weaken the united

